# Kitty6 renderer mods: rules of our own, read by crates/victory-gpu/src/kitty6.rs.
# A rule names a translated shader by its runtime hash (as the log and
# `victory replay --timing detailed` print it) and says what to do with the
# draws and dispatches that use it. Nothing of the title is in this file.
#
#   <16 hex digits> skip              never run
#   <16 hex digits> every <n>         run in one frame of n (results stay in place between)
#   <16 hex digits> every <n> at <k>  ... in frames whose number % n == k
#
# scripts\play.ps1 passes every mods\*.k6mod unless -NoMods. In game, F4 then
# the MODS item turns all rules off and on (VICTORY_DEV=<s>:mods in a script).

# 02384a60fda6f2d0: one 1x1x1 compute dispatch that costs ~10.9 ms a frame on
# NVIDIA (a 64-lane program run as a single group). Skipping it outright bought
# ~3 fps with no visible change in the opening scene. A single-group pass is
# often an average (exposure-style), so run it every 4th frame instead of never.
02384a60fda6f2d0 every 4
